## Commands (always use these, never ad-hoc tool invocations)

- `make setup` — install dependencies from the lockfile <!-- kept: none -->
- `make format` — auto-format <!-- kept: none -->
- `make lint` — lint + format check <!-- kept: none -->
- `make typecheck` — strict type check <!-- kept: none -->
- `make test` — run tests <!-- kept: none -->
- `make gen` — regenerate types from `ontology/` (never edit generated files) <!-- kept: word -->
- `make ontology` — check `ontology/` + `wiki/` consistency and generated code <!-- kept: none -->
- `make check` — everything CI runs. **Run it before you say a task is done.** <!-- kept: word -->

## Before you change code

1. Read `wiki/index.md` to orient yourself. `wiki/log.md`, `wiki/index.md` and `ontology/glossary.md`
   are drawn by `make derived`; edit the fragments, not the drawn files. If one is missing, run
   `make derived`. <!-- kept: word -->
2. If the task touches business logic, read `ontology/glossary.md` and the
   relevant `ontology/entities/*.yaml`. <!-- kept: none -->
3. Look for an existing implementation of the rule before writing a new one.
   Every business rule should live in exactly one place. <!-- kept: word -->

## Rules

- Use the names from `ontology/glossary.md`. Do not invent synonyms
  (e.g. `Client` when the glossary says `Customer`). <!-- kept: word -->
- Use the generated domain types; to change them, change `ontology/` and run `make gen`. <!-- kept: word -->
- Do not add a new entity, relation or rule to the code without adding it to
  `ontology/` in the same change. Changes to `ontology/` change what the business
  means: call them out in the PR description. <!-- kept: word -->
- Every behaviour change comes with a test. <!-- kept: word -->
- Never commit secrets. <!-- kept: secret-scan -->
- Never commit `.env`. Configuration goes in `.env.example`. <!-- kept: word -->
- Keep changes small and focused; one concern per PR. <!-- kept: word -->
- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`). <!-- kept: commit-format -->

## After you finish a task

- `make check` is green. <!-- kept: word -->
- Update the wiki: <!-- kept: word -->
  - `make log m="what changed — link to PR/issue"` adds one entry to the wiki log: one new file in
    `wiki/log/`, so two branches never edit the same line; <!-- kept: none -->
  - a new term: `python3 tools/ledgers.py add-term <Term> --definition "..."`; <!-- kept: none -->
  - a new wiki page needs only `type` and `title` in its front matter: the index lists it by itself.
    If `wiki/index.md` is still in git (this repository has not split it yet), add the link there; <!-- kept: none -->
  - significant technical choice → new `wiki/decisions/NNNN-title.md`; <!-- kept: word -->
  - production bug or outage → `wiki/incidents/YYYY-MM-DD-title.md`; <!-- kept: word -->
  - an entity's behaviour changed → update `wiki/entities/<entity>.md`. <!-- kept: word -->
- Follow the page formats in `ontology/page-types.yaml`. <!-- kept: wiki-format -->
- Link to code paths, do not paste code into the wiki. <!-- kept: word -->

